gosh seam 06: The core's two mains get other names, so that gosh's main runs first.

For:   REQ10/SHAPE-1, REQ6/NAME-1. gosh's words (its options, and later its names and first
       words) are taken out of the arguments by gosh's own main, in src/seam, which then calls
       the core's main with only what a stock mosh would have been given. So no option of
       gosh's is parsed inside the core, and a moved pin cannot break one.
What:  main becomes mosh_client_main in mosh-client.cc and mosh_server_main in mosh-server.cc;
       each file includes the header that declares them.
       The client's print_colorcount stops being private to its file, because the command
       is given it to call (it is what "mosh-client -c" prints).
Where: mosh-client.cc; mosh-server.cc.
Kind:  one line changed and one added in each, and one word (static) removed. Nothing is moved.
Needs: 05-build, which links the library holding gosh's main into each program.
From:  written for gosh.
Pin:   upstream mosh at decd9b705eb81626f694335b8d5940538beb06da; cut against the result of the patch before it.

